// S9, an accepted imprecision: two stores to one destination merge, so `y.f = x; y.f = w`
// sends `x.g` to `w.g`. The first store's labels at `y.f.g` are `All`, as they must be for
// `l = y; l.f = x` to reach `y.f.g`.
//
// The index moves a label backward only along copy chains rooted at a formal and at program
// stores, and `y.f` is neither, so the engines do not derive this:
// parity: backward alias rule loses: TwoStoresMerge: sink(%S)#0 <- %S
def TwoStoresMerge() {
s:
  x.g = source(S);
  y.f = x;
  y.f = w;
  z = w.g;
  sink(z, S);
  return;
}

// The observable, every sink each label reaches:
// expect: TwoStoresMerge: sink(%S)#0 <- %S
